course: dictionary
lesson: 2519
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word deck is a good example. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which is the context.
explain: «4 players get 7 cards each from a full deck: 4 × 7 = 28 dealt, so 52 − 28 = 24 cards are left.» The words cards, players and dealt show that deck means a set of playing cards.
explain: «The sailors stood on the deck of the ship.» Here the words ship and sailors show that deck means a floor on a ship. Always ask which meaning fits the story, then try it in the sentence to check.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A deck can be a set of playing cards, a floor on a ship or bus, a wooden floor outside a house, or a verb meaning to decorate.
fact: A usual deck of cards has 52 cards, in 4 suits of 13.
fact: To deck is to decorate, as in «deck the halls».
fact: The top deck of a bus is the upper floor of the bus.
exercise: «4 players get 7 cards each from a full deck: 4 × 7 = 28 dealt, so 52 − 28 = 24 cards are left.» In this sentence, what is a deck? | To decorate with lights | A floor on a ship | A wooden floor outside a house | *A set of playing cards
exercise: Mia says, «Let's deck the halls with paper chains.» What does deck mean here? | *To decorate | A set of playing cards | A wooden floor outside a house | A floor of a bus
exercise: «The sailors stood on the deck of the ship.» Which meaning of deck fits? | *A floor of a ship | To decorate | A set of 52 cards | A kind of boat
test: Dad sat on the deck in the summer sun. What is the deck? | To decorate | A ship's engine | A set of playing cards | *A wooden floor outside the house
test: A usual deck of cards has how many cards? | 13 | 24 | 4 | *52
exam: In the sentence «We sat on the top deck of the bus and waved», what does deck mean? | *A floor of a bus | To decorate | A set of playing cards | A type of sailing boat
